24.9.
What's built: --modular-magnitude-update multiplicative. With it, each DoRA magnitude scalar moves by a fraction of its own value per step, rather than a fixed amount: m ← m·exp(−lr·sign). So a 0.13 scalar moves as carefully as a 2.4 one, and none can go negative. The default stays additive, so existing recipes behave exactly as before. Commits: 3197c28 (optimizer + tests), a7de168 (trainer flag), plus manual updates.
